text:
This Node.js function is supposed to look up a user's plan tier and apply a discount, but it throws in production for some users. Find the bug and fix it.

```javascript
function applyDiscount(user, plans) {
  const plan = plans.find(p => p.id === user.planId);
  const discountRate = plan.discountRate;
  return user.total * (1 - discountRate);
}

applyDiscount({ planId: 'legacy-99', total: 200 }, [{ id: 'basic', discountRate: 0.1 }]);
```

